TEXT 64 -232 Left 3 ;#110 Flexible 555 ramp generator
TEXT 64 -168 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bVahBmsvirE
TEXT 64 -120 Left 2 ;The 555 resets a current-charged ramp; two amplifier stages set its amplitude and DC offset.
TEXT 2200 48 Left 2 !.ic V(RAMP)=0
TEXT 2200 96 Left 2 !.tran 0 600m 0 20u
TEXT 2200 168 Left 2 !.meas tran RAMP_LO MIN V(RAMP) FROM 200m TO 600m
TEXT 2200 216 Left 2 !.meas tran RAMP_HI MAX V(RAMP) FROM 200m TO 600m
TEXT 2200 264 Left 2 !.meas tran TS1 WHEN V(RAMP)=4.5 TD=200m RISE=1
TEXT 2200 312 Left 2 !.meas tran TS2 WHEN V(RAMP)=4.5 TD=200m RISE=2
TEXT 2200 360 Left 2 !.meas tran SWEEP_PERIOD PARAM TS2-TS1
TEXT 2200 408 Left 2 !.meas tran TR_LO WHEN V(RAMP)=4 TD=200m RISE=1
TEXT 2200 456 Left 2 !.meas tran TR_HI WHEN V(RAMP)=5 TD=200m RISE=1
TEXT 2200 504 Left 2 !.meas tran ICHARGE PARAM 22u/(TR_HI-TR_LO)
TEXT 2200 552 Left 2 !.meas tran OUT_LO MIN V(OUT) FROM 200m TO 600m
TEXT 2200 600 Left 2 !.meas tran OUT_HI MAX V(OUT) FROM 200m TO 600m
TEXT 2200 648 Left 2 !.meas tran INV1_LO MIN V(INV1) FROM 200m TO 600m
TEXT 2200 696 Left 2 !.meas tran INV1_HI MAX V(INV1) FROM 200m TO 600m
TEXT 2200 784 Left 2 ;Alan's example timing capacitor is 22u. The speed, gain and\noffset controls are set to the middle of their 5k ranges, so the\nplot shows one setting of an adjustable circuit, not a fixed design.
TEXT 2200 912 Left 2 ;The 555 is LTspice's NE555 macromodel. U1A and U1B are the two\nhalves of one LM358, a part Alan names on his drawing.
